From: Chris Sotraidis <56282582+chrissotraidis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:13:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] port: the front-end scene a host can name as a number

The overlay already receives the scene label the front end formats, and
the label begins with the scene number, so the number was in reach but
only as text. A host that has to tell "the game moved" apart from "the
pad carried a bit" needs the engine's own answer to the first question,
and re-parsing the label outside this file would tie a host to a format
this file writes.

Parsed where the format lives, and only when the label really begins
with a digit, because 0 is a scene (SCENE_FRIENDLY_BACKGROUND) and so
cannot double as "no scene".
---
 smstrikers-port/include/port/overlay.h   |  4 ++++
 smstrikers-port/src/platform/overlay.cpp | 14 +++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smstrikers-port/include/port/overlay.h b/smstrikers-port/include/port/overlay.h
index 4f08e1a..906861d 100644
--- a/smstrikers-port/include/port/overlay.h
+++ b/smstrikers-port/include/port/overlay.h
@@ -22,6 +22,10 @@ void PortOverlaySetMatch(float clock, int scoreHome, int scoreAway);
 // The last of those labels, read back; the control channel's heartbeat prints it and has no window
 // to draw into. Never NULL.
 const char* PortOverlaySceneName(void);
+// The scene number the label begins with, as the engine recorded it: -1 before the first scene.
+// A host that has to tell "the game moved" apart from "the pad carried a bit" needs the engine's
+// own answer to the first question, and this is it rather than a host re-parsing the label.
+int PortOverlaySceneNumber(void);
 void PortOverlayToggleMenu(void);
 int  PortOverlayMenuOpen(void);
 void PortOverlayHandleKey(int scancode, int down);
diff --git a/smstrikers-port/src/platform/overlay.cpp b/smstrikers-port/src/platform/overlay.cpp
index 811eaa4..2ed6037 100644
--- a/smstrikers-port/src/platform/overlay.cpp
+++ b/smstrikers-port/src/platform/overlay.cpp
@@ -92,6 +92,9 @@ int s_read;
 
 char s_scene[64] = "-";
 char s_stadium[64] = "-";
+// PORT: the number inside the label above. -1 before any scene, and the overlay's one place that
+// knows the label's shape, so a host reads the number rather than parsing a string written here.
+int s_sceneNumber = -1;
 float s_clock;
 int s_scoreHome, s_scoreAway;
 
@@ -391,8 +394,17 @@ int PortOverlayEnabled(void)
     return s_enabled;
 }
 
-void PortOverlaySetScene(const char* name) { copy_into(s_scene, sizeof(s_scene), name); }
+void PortOverlaySetScene(const char* name)
+{
+    copy_into(s_scene, sizeof(s_scene), name);
+    // The label carries the number first (BaseGameSceneManager formats it), and it is parsed with
+    // the format rather than by each reader of it.
+    s_sceneNumber = (name != nullptr && name[0] >= '0' && name[0] <= '9')
+                        ? (int)std::strtol(name, nullptr, 10)
+                        : -1;
+}
 const char* PortOverlaySceneName(void) { return s_scene; }
+int PortOverlaySceneNumber(void) { return s_sceneNumber; }
 void PortOverlaySetStadium(const char* name)
 {
     copy_into(s_stadium, sizeof(s_stadium), name);
